1. git init----to initialize git repository 
2. git config---to store the details or set or controls the variables
3. git add---add the file into staging area  
4. git status- to check the status of file 
5. git commit -m "message".---to commit file into remote repo
6. git push -u origin "branch"---to push the file from local to remote repo branch
7. git log or git log --oneline---to find all the commits in repo
8. git pull--- to sync the files and download from remote to local repo
9. git fetch---to download the file from remote to local without making changes
10.git clone- to to get the repository from remote to local
11.git cherry "ID"---to pick particular commits from one branch to other without whole files and sync
12.git merge---sync all the branches in local 
13.git fetch---sync all the brances in local with clean history
14.git amend---to add any info inside the file which is commited before pushed into remote repo
15.git reset---to delete the file from local repo after commit to remote and the files will be deleted 
16.git reset --soft "ID"---delets the file in local repo but still shows in working/local
17.git reset --hard "ID" ---deletes the file from local repo completely
18.git reset --mixed "ID"---deleted the file but still shows in staging area
19: git revert---deletes the file but still shows in the commits that has done and can undo that

















 
